course: dictionary
lesson: 10332
title: A trainee is still learning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A trainee is a person who is being taught how to do a job. The word tells you that the person is still learning and is not yet fully skilled. The words around it give clues: a trainee teacher is learning to teach.
explain: «Keepers usually start as volunteers or trainees, and the job needs knowledge, safety and lots of patience.» Here trainees are people at the start of the job, learning from experienced keepers. The clue words start and volunteers show they are new to it.
explain: «Many trainees never become stars at all.» This sentence is about K-pop singers who train for years before their first show. Trainees are learning the skills, and not everyone who trains goes on to succeed.
fact: A trainee is a person who is being taught how to do a job.
fact: Trainee is a noun: one trainee, two trainees.
fact: You can put trainee before a noun, as in trainee teacher, trainee nurse, trainee pilot or trainee chef.
fact: A trainee is still learning, so they are not yet fully experienced.
fact: «Trainees» can be people in many jobs, from keepers and nurses to singers and drivers.
exercise: What is a trainee? | A person who never does any work | *A person who is being taught how to do a job | A person who has retired from a job | A person who runs a company
exercise: «Keepers usually start as volunteers or trainees.» In this sentence, what are trainees? | *People who are still learning the job | Animals that live in the zoo | Bosses who give orders | Visitors who buy tickets
exercise: What does trainee mean in «trainee nurse»? | A nurse who has worked for forty years | A nurse who is on holiday | A hospital bed | *A nurse who is still learning the job
test: A trainee pilot is learning to do what? | *Fly planes | Cook meals | Build houses | Teach children
test: Which word means a person who is being taught a job? | garden | *trainee | teacher | pilot
exam: Which sentence uses trainee correctly? | *The trainee chef was learning to cut onions safely. | The trainee chef owned the kitchen and gave all the orders. | The trainee chef was a famous judge on television. | The trainee chef had cooked in five top restaurants for years.
